      "content": "That's much more readable, thank you. I think this version will actually help the client understand the concept.\n\nWait, I just got an alert from the senior partner. They ran your second version through the keyword tool and the score dropped significantly—almost to zero. They're worried that because the summary is too \"plain,\" it's missing the specific technical and legal identifiers that prove the patent's novelty is being captured. They basically said if the summary doesn't hit the claim terms, they can't even sign off on it to send to the client.\n\nIs there a way you can rewrite this so it's still clear and easy to read, but you find a way to weave those specific technical terms back in? I really need to find a middle ground where it's understandable but still hits a high enough score on the tool so the partners don't reject it. Just try to balance the two without making it a total wall of text again.",
